#!/bin/sh
# Refuse to put development material on the shipped branch.
#
# `omarchy plugin add` clones the whole repository into a user's shell config, so
# the shipped branch carries the plugin, its tests and the operator documentation
# only (DEVIATIONS.md R11, R13).
#
# The check keys on the *branch name* `master`, never on "the default branch":
# since R13 the default branch is `dev`, the integration branch that carries all
# of this material on purpose, and a guard keyed on the default branch would
# refuse every normal commit. The name and the path lists both come from
# tests/lib/shipped-paths.sh, which the gate suite and the release sync read too.
#
# Install once per clone — as a copy into .git/hooks/, not via core.hooksPath:
#
#   cp .githooks/pre-commit .git/hooks/pre-commit && chmod +x .git/hooks/pre-commit
#
# `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` looks tidier and is what this repo used
# to document, but it goes inert exactly where it matters: `.githooks/` is
# denylisted, so checking out `master` removes the directory and git then finds
# no hook to run. .git/ belongs to no branch, so a copy there survives the
# switch. It does go stale — re-copy it when this file changes. The two guards
# that cannot go stale are `tests/branch-model.test.sh` (in the gate, and
# shipped on `master` too) and `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.
#
# Bypass deliberately:  OMAFAN_ALLOW_DEV_PATHS=1 git commit ...
set -u

[ "${OMAFAN_ALLOW_DEV_PATHS:-0}" = "1" ] && exit 0

branch=$(git symbolic-ref --quiet --short HEAD 2>/dev/null || echo "")
# Detached HEAD (rebase, cherry-pick, the release sync's worktree) and every
# feature branch are someone else's problem; only the shipped branch is guarded,
# and it is checked *before* the lists are required so that a branch without
# them — an old one, or one predating this hook — is never blocked.
#
# The shipped branch's name is the one fact this hook needs before it can read
# the lists, so it also appears here as a literal. tests/lib/shipped-paths.sh is
# its home and tests/branch-model.test.sh asserts the two agree.
[ "$branch" = "master" ] || exit 0

repo=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || echo "")
lists="$repo/tests/lib/shipped-paths.sh"
if [ ! -r "$lists" ]; then
    # Fail closed, but only here: on the shipped branch, without the lists, this
    # hook cannot tell shipped from development material, and guessing is the one
    # mistake it exists to prevent.
    printf 'pre-commit: cannot read %s — refusing to guess on %s.\n' "$lists" "$branch" >&2
    printf '  restore the file, or: OMAFAN_ALLOW_DEV_PATHS=1 git commit ...\n' >&2
    exit 1
fi
# shellcheck source=tests/lib/shipped-paths.sh
. "$lists"

[ "$branch" = "$OMAFAN_SHIPPED_BRANCH" ] || exit 0

staged=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACMR)
offenders=$(printf '%s\n' "$staged" | omafan_dev_paths_in)
[ -n "$offenders" ] || exit 0

printf 'pre-commit: refusing to commit development material on %s\n\n' "$branch" >&2
printf '%s\n' "$offenders" | sed 's/^/  /' >&2
cat >&2 <<'MSG'

These paths exist to develop omafan and must never reach the shipped branch:
users clone it into ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/<id> (DEVIATIONS.md R11, R13).

    git switch dev      # land the change there instead

A release does not merge dev; it copies the shipped path allowlist:

    skills/publish-a-release/sync-master.sh --from dev

Deliberate override: OMAFAN_ALLOW_DEV_PATHS=1 git commit ...
MSG
exit 1
